; t15_shared.ent — v14 shared variables: plain names, cross-body visibility,
; and transparent atomicity across threads. Four spawned workers each do
; 25000 atomic `cnt++` increments; the final count must be exactly 100000
; (a lost update or torn cell would corrupt it). Worker 4 also maintains a
; second counter with plain read-modify-write — correct single-writer, and
; it proves ordinary shared reads/writes work in spawned bodies.
; (spawn returns its chan on the stack; binds are pass-through, so each
; spawn is bound immediately.)
; Expected: count: 100000, count2: 25000.
0 cnt!
0 cnt2!
'w1 spawn c1!
'w2 spawn c2!
'w3 spawn c3!
'w4 spawn c4!
c1@ dequeue c2@ dequeue c3@ dequeue c4@ dequeue 'join4 for
"count: " print cnt@ print
"count2: " print cnt2@ print
ret
w1: 25000 'bump for ret
w2: 25000 'bump for ret
w3: 25000 'bump for ret
w4: 25000 'both for ret
bump: k! cnt++ ret
both: k! cnt++ cnt2@ 1 add cnt2! ret
join4: q! q@ ret
